{
  "dom_id": "step-33555",
  "name": "Example: \n                    The Volume of a Cube: Word Problems",
  "problem": "Six identical plastic cubic containers have a combined volume of $48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3.$ Find the side length of a single container.",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the volume of a single container: \n\n$$\n\\dfrac{48 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3}{6} = 8 \\: \\textrm{ft}^3\n$$\n\nNow, we need to find the side length of one container. \n\nSince the volume of a cube is \n\n$$\nV = s^3,\n$$\n\nwhere $s$ is the length of a side, we can find $s$ as follows:\n\n$$\ns = \\sqrt[3]{V} = \\sqrt[3]{8} = 2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of a side of a single container is $2\\,\\textrm{ft}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
